{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/421257-inquisition-and-malleus","id":421257,"title":"Inquisition and Malleus","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-26T22:03:57-08:00","id":421257,"title":"Inquisition and Malleus","content":"So the setting probably won't happen, given how Ptolemaic Mummy is trouncing it in the poll - but it is interesting to ponder. Specifically, given the history we know from Doubting Souls, and the summary of the Inquisition making Spain hostile to the Vigil. I was considering whether Benedictions predate Malleus (which won't be formed yet in this era, but is right over the horizon), and I have an idea...<br /> <br /> While Cardinal Torchemada and Queen Isabella are 100% mortal and not under any supernatural influence, there is a point of corruption high up the Church hierarchy with influence in the Inquisition, intentionally pointing it at Hunters - a Ghoul by the name of Ambrogio Baudolino.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile specifically targeted by the Inquisition (along with Ascending Ones and other Conversos - and of course the Lucifuge), are small groups of Catholic &quot;Heretics&quot; who practice Benedictions in their Vigil (so individual cells not even Tier 2 in scale, but having discovered a Tier 3 Endowment).<br /> <br /> The era would culminated in Baudilno destroying his master, possibly with assistance from the Lucifuge herself, and reversing his positions in the Church to now become the active protector of those Benediction wielding Hunters...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T23:10:44-08:00","id":421359,"title":"","content":"The Spanish Inquisition chapter was/is supposed to take place in the 1600s, which actually makes it concurrent with the era in Lily, Saber, and Thorn, and Doubting Souls, just in a different country. (That said, several people argued it <i>should</i> have been 15th century...)<br /> <br /> In a sense, it could have made a decent historical bridge, if written to do so, with Requiem For Regina flowing into Spanish Inquisition flowing into Lily, Saber, and Thorn flowing into Doubting Souls. If you add a Protestant Reformation era before that, and a Napoleonic Era afterwards, you could make a continuous stream of settings reflecting the end of the Middle Ages and the dawn of the Early Modern Era. In fact, Brothers Grimm, Victorian Lost, Russian Revolution, Handful of Dust, God's Own Country, and Bowry Dogs basically just form a chain straight up to the modern day from there... Just missing World War II itself, and then the giant gaping hole of the Renaissance. <br /> <br /> I know it's not going to happen, but I'd like it if they rearranged the chapters to be in chronological order, and put in at least some lines that help link one chapter to the next, so that it can be viewed as the flow of history, rather than hermetically sealed chambers all to their lonesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T23:19:58-08:00","id":421365,"title":"","content":"Oh, that changed since it was first up and it was in the late 1400s (i.e. in the era of Isabella and Torquemada) - well I've definitely lost a point of interest in it (getting to see Catholic Hunter pre-Malleus).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T07:06:07-08:00","id":421722,"title":"","content":"The 1600s does not seem accurate to me, either. Where was this posted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T07:17:41-08:00","id":421730,"title":"","content":"On the poll itself it says 1600s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T07:32:09-08:00","id":421737,"title":"","content":"Ah, you're right. I was just surprised to hear the interpretation was an overlap with Doubting Souls. Our Era takes place in the 1690s, so anything from the Spanish Inquisition Era would precede our chapter. The SI has a 200 year history, which would no doubt be covered to put the new Era in context similar to how the other writers designed their chapters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T08:04:23-08:00","id":421761,"title":"","content":"Longer than 200 years actually. The last known victim of the Inquisition was a school master accused of teaching Deism in 1826.<br /> <br /> Given that was after the Inquisition had sputtered in and out of existence for a while during the Napolronic Wars and said execution was effectively the last straw for the educated elite in the royal court who saw it officially disbanded once and for all soon after.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T08:42:42-08:00","id":421794,"title":"","content":"Sure, but most of the activity for the SI, what it's known for, is during that time frame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}